A||||6||1FieroGTRacingInc||Steering Column.....||||1||
Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||04-04-2000||07:38 AM||||Hey everybody.... I have a case of the *wobble* in my tilt....  What column's, from what vehicles, WILL FIT our Fiero's??  thank's for your time???   1FGTRInc.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-04-2000||09:07 AM||||Check the older cavaliers 6000 and small olds cutlass like ciera. An interchange book should say.<P>if you have automatic tranny be very careful handling the end of the shift interlock cable or parts will fly. bag the end of the cable while you work on anything else. Even if it's only a few minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||N_Man||04-04-2000||12:06 PM||||I have the same problem in mine. A mechanic told me it was likly a loose screw in the steering column (I think take off the steering wheel and all the other controls to get at it. I think) but he wanted about 3 hours of labour to fix it. For a loose screw i didn't think it was worthwhile. Could do it myself when I get the time.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||04-04-2000||04:35 PM||||It probably is 4 loose screws down inside the column behind the steering wheel.  It is possible to tighten 3 of them without completely removing the upper part of the column, but you have to be careful and notice how all the parts fit as you dig down through the layers.  It's kind of a pain, but cheaper than buying another column.  This is a very typical problem with General Motors and some Chrysler stuff that use the same design.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-04-2000||06:18 PM||||I have a page for fixing it. I really don't recomend most people fix it, especially if you have to buy the tools. <P>If you aren't very careful digging down and putting it back together you can make a major mess. The counter balance spring can hurt you. You can break things pretty easy.<P>The 4 offending screws need to be taken out, cleaned, and Locktite(tm) put on them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||04-04-2000||08:49 PM||||Thank's guy's...  After hearing all that ... I'll go find another column...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR>                          1FGTRInc.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TOM||04-04-2000||09:25 PM||||I just tightened my wobble problem. It took about 20 minutes and less than 10 in special tools.||||reg||1
